  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What is the best time of year to enjoy seafood in Nha Trang?",
      "answer": "The best time to enjoy seafood in Nha Trang is generally during the dry season, from February to August. During these months, the weather is sunny, and the sea is calm, which ensures a more abundant and diverse catch for the restaurants. However, fresh seafood is available year-round, with certain species being more plentiful in different seasons."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is Nha Trang seafood expensive?",
      "answer": "Compared to Western countries, Nha Trang seafood is generally very affordable. Prices vary greatly depending on the type of seafood (e.g., lobster is pricier than clams), the preparation method, and the restaurant's ambiance. You can enjoy a generous seafood meal at a local eatery for VND 150,000-300,000 ($6-12), while more upscale restaurants will naturally cost more."
    },
    {
      "question": "How do I ensure the seafood is fresh?",
      "answer": "The best way to ensure freshness is to choose restaurants where you can pick your own live seafood from tanks. Look for clear water, active fish and shellfish, and no unpleasant odors. Most reputable seafood restaurants in Nha Trang pride themselves on serving only the freshest catch, often sourced directly from local fishermen daily."
    },
    {
      "question": "What are some must-try Nha Trang seafood dishes?",
      "answer": "Beyond grilled fish and prawns, you should definitely try the local specialties like grilled lobster with garlic butter, steamed giant clams (ốc móng tay), blood cockles (sò huyết) stir-fried with tamarind, and the famous Nha Trang fish noodle soup (bún chả cá). Don't miss out on various snails (ốc) prepared in different flavorful sauces."
    },
    {
      "question": "Are there vegetarian or non-seafood options available at these restaurants?",
      "answer": "While these venues specialize in seafood, most larger restaurants will offer some basic non-seafood options, such as stir-fried vegetables, rice dishes, or sometimes chicken and pork dishes. Smaller, more specialized seafood stalls might have limited non-seafood choices, so it's always best to check the menu or ask beforehand if you have specific dietary needs."
    },
    {
      "question": "Should I be careful about hygiene when eating street seafood in Nha Trang?",
      "answer": "While generally safe, it's always wise to exercise some caution, especially with street food. Look for stalls with high customer turnover, ensuring ingredients are cooked fresh to order. Ensure seafood is thoroughly cooked and avoid raw preparations if you have a sensitive stomach. Stick to bottled water to minimize any risks."
    }
